menu "Station: availability ledger"

    config LEDGER_TARGET_PERMILLE
        int "Daily graced-uptime target (per mille)"
        range 900 1000
        default 998
        help
            Graced uptime the protected (Onocoy) slot needs per UTC day.
            Onocoy's streak needs Availability >= 0.98, which on its scoring
            curve means a graced uptime of 99.8 %: with the daily grant below
            that is about 473 s of downtime per UTC day at a perfect data
            rate (a plain 98 % uptime would score only about 0.81).

    config LEDGER_GRACE_S
        int "Daily downtime grant of the protected slot (s)"
        range 0 3600
        default 300
        help
            Seconds Onocoy adds to each day's uptime before scoring it.

    config LEDGER_HISTORY_DAYS
        int "Days of per-day history kept"
        range 7 90
        default 30

    config LEDGER_ALIVE_PERSIST_S
        int "Persist the last-alive mark every (s)"
        range 10 600
        default 60
        help
            After a power cut, the time between this mark and the next boot
            is counted as downtime. Shorter is more exact but writes NVS
            more often (60 s is about 1500 page erases per page in 10 years
            with the 112 KB NVS partition).

endmenu
